<title>LITHUANIA: GOVERNMENT REFUSES ANDREKIENE RESIGNATION.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT REFUSES ANDREKIENE RESIGNATION.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government on Monday said it has rejected the resignation of European Affairs Minister Laime Andrikiene as chairman of the foreign loans commission.</p>
<p>&quot;The statement of resignation of Laima Andrikiene from the position of chairman of the state foreign loans commission will not be discussed in the government,&quot; the government press office said in a statement.</p>
<p>The ministry said on Friday that Andrikiene wanted to quit the commission as she said the loans were being used inefficiently.</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom, +370 2 223 517</p>
